# Borders - Essential Rules

## ✅ ALWAYS Use Inline Styles for Borders

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Inline styles with design system colors
<div className="bg-card p-4 rounded-lg" style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
<div style={{ border: "2px dashed var(--border)" }}>
<div style={{ borderTop: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
```

## ⚠️ Why Not Tailwind Border Classes

Tailwind v4's `border` class sets `border-width: 0px` by default, making borders invisible.

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - No visible border
<div className="border border-border">

// ✅ CORRECT - Visible border
<div style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
```

## 🎯 Common Border Patterns

```tsx
// Standard border
style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}

// Thick border
style={{ border: "2px solid var(--border)" }}

// Dashed border
style={{ border: "1px dashed var(--border)" }}

// Top border only
style={{ borderTop: "2px solid var(--border)" }}
```

## 🎯 Key Rule

**Borders are the ONLY exception** to the "maximize Tailwind classes" rule due to Tailwind v4 limitations.

